[
  {
    "segment_id": "SRR_001_0",
    "start": 6.861,
    "end": 12.806,
    "original_speaker": "SPEAKER_00",
    "verified_speaker": "Translator",
    "text": "So the arisal of a particular thought is not an integral part or an inherent part.",
    "include_in_corpus": null,
    "exclusion_reason": null
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "SRR_001_1",
    "start": 13.487,
    "end": 18.311,
    "original_speaker": "SPEAKER_00",
    "verified_speaker": "Translator",
    "text": "It's not one and the same, if you will, with the natural state of mind itself.",
    "include_in_corpus": null,
    "exclusion_reason": null
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "SRR_001_2",
    "start": 19.692,
    "end": 32.142,
    "original_speaker": "SPEAKER_00",
    "verified_speaker": "Translator",
    "text": "So if a thought isn't an inherently existent part of one's mind, then its ending or its cessation can similarly not be an integral or inherent part of mind.",
    "include_in_corpus": null,
    "exclusion_reason": null
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "SRR_001_3",
    "start": 32.843,
    "end": 35.025,
    "original_speaker": "SPEAKER_00",
    "verified_speaker": "Translator",
    "text": "As such, what to talk about is its remaining.",
    "include_in_corpus": null,
    "exclusion_reason": null
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "SRR_001_4",
    "start": 36.167,
    "end": 39.229,
    "original_speaker": "SPEAKER_00",
    "verified_speaker": "Translator",
    "text": "So then the question is, do thoughts not exist at all?",
    "include_in_corpus": null,
    "exclusion_reason": null
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "SRR_001_5",
    "start": 39.73,
    "end": 42.011,
    "original_speaker": "SPEAKER_00",
    "verified_speaker": "Translator",
    "text": "They exist but they don't truly exist.",
    "include_in_corpus": null,
    "exclusion_reason": null
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "SRR_001_6",
    "start": 63.607,
    "end": 90.282,
    "original_speaker": "SPEAKER_00",
    "verified_speaker": "Translator",
    "text": "And so, for example, when we think about then the way that there is no inherent arising or cessation of thoughts integral to then the nature of one's mind, then with regard to mind itself, mind itself cannot be neither benefited nor harmed by the arisal or then the cessation of these seemingly tangible, seemingly integral paths",
    "include_in_corpus": null,
    "exclusion_reason": null
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "SRR_001_7",
    "start": 91.503,
    "end": 93.526,
    "original_speaker": "SPEAKER_00",
    "verified_speaker": "Translator",
    "text": "of our being, of these thoughts, if you will.",
    "include_in_corpus": null,
    "exclusion_reason": null
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "SRR_001_8",
    "start": 94.207,
    "end": 100.776,
    "original_speaker": "SPEAKER_00",
    "verified_speaker": "Translator",
    "text": "As such, we can notice the thoughts arising then, but then they will have no effect on our true nature.",
    "include_in_corpus": null,
    "exclusion_reason": null
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "SRR_001_9",
    "start": 100.976,
    "end": 106.625,
    "original_speaker": "SPEAKER_00",
    "verified_speaker": "Translator",
    "text": "As such, the advice is given then to simply rest in the true nature of mind.",
    "include_in_corpus": null,
    "exclusion_reason": null
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "SRR_001_10",
    "start": 108.198,
    "end": 112.642,
    "original_speaker": "SPEAKER_01",
    "verified_speaker": "Rinpochoe",
    "text": "This then is the experience of the bare natural state, the way it is now.",
    "include_in_corpus": null,
    "exclusion_reason": null
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "SRR_001_11",
    "start": 112.702,
    "end": 117.125,
    "original_speaker": "SPEAKER_01",
    "verified_speaker": "Rinpochoe",
    "text": "If you take that empty awareness that is open and carefree as the path,",
    "include_in_corpus": null,
    "exclusion_reason": null
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "SRR_001_12",
    "start": 133.083,
    "end": 146.487,
    "original_speaker": "SPEAKER_00",
    "verified_speaker": "Translator",
    "text": "All the time, both during formal meditation practice and also afterward, in the post-meditation time, you will quickly and surely acquire a confident realization that confusion is freed by itself.",
    "include_in_corpus": null,
    "exclusion_reason": null
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "SRR_001_13",
    "start": 160.144,
    "end": 162.105,
    "original_speaker": "SPEAKER_01",
    "verified_speaker": "Rinpochoe",
    "text": "So here then, there are two things to bear in mind.",
    "include_in_corpus": null,
    "exclusion_reason": null
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "SRR_001_14",
    "start": 177.733,
    "end": 193.24,
    "original_speaker": "SPEAKER_00",
    "verified_speaker": "Translator",
    "text": "So the empty kind of awareness, that is then the formal kind of meditation practice, if you will, simply to remain within that bare natural state the way it is, open and carefree, and that's our kind of spiritual path, if you will.",
    "include_in_corpus": null,
    "exclusion_reason": null
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "SRR_001_15",
    "start": 194.52,
    "end": 197.982,
    "original_speaker": "SPEAKER_00",
    "verified_speaker": "Translator",
    "text": "But when it comes to post-meditation period,",
    "include_in_corpus": null,
    "exclusion_reason": null
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "SRR_001_16",
    "start": 198.751,
    "end": 210.917,
    "original_speaker": "SPEAKER_00",
    "verified_speaker": "Translator",
    "text": "the afterward, if you will, of the formal meditation practice, then it is essential to, at all times and in all situations, as much as one is possible, to look at then the nature of mind.",
    "include_in_corpus": null,
    "exclusion_reason": null
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "SRR_001_17",
    "start": 211.337,
    "end": 214.839,
    "original_speaker": "SPEAKER_00",
    "verified_speaker": "Translator",
    "text": "Look at when thoughts arise, to simply look at their nature.",
    "include_in_corpus": null,
    "exclusion_reason": null
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "SRR_001_18",
    "start": 215.44,
    "end": 221.963,
    "original_speaker": "SPEAKER_00",
    "verified_speaker": "Translator",
    "text": "And this is similar then to the formal meditation practice, where one sustains the empty awareness, the nature of the mind.",
    "include_in_corpus": null,
    "exclusion_reason": null
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "SRR_001_19",
    "start": 222.283,
    "end": 227.726,
    "original_speaker": "SPEAKER_00",
    "verified_speaker": "Translator",
    "text": "So as such, during the post-meditation period, as much as one is able, one looks at the nature",
    "include_in_corpus": null,
    "exclusion_reason": null
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "SRR_001_20",
    "start": 228.607,
    "end": 229.668,
    "original_speaker": "SPEAKER_00",
    "verified_speaker": "Translator",
    "text": "of one's mind.",
    "include_in_corpus": null,
    "exclusion_reason": null
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "SRR_001_21",
    "start": 230.55,
    "end": 233.374,
    "original_speaker": "SPEAKER_01",
    "verified_speaker": "Rinpochoe",
    "text": "So something to do when you get stuck in the New York traffic.",
    "include_in_corpus": null,
    "exclusion_reason": null
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "SRR_001_22",
    "start": 244.157,
    "end": 245.077,
    "original_speaker": "SPEAKER_01",
    "verified_speaker": "Rinpochoe",
    "text": "So I'm not really joking here.",
    "include_in_corpus": null,
    "exclusion_reason": null
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "SRR_001_23",
    "start": 245.097,
    "end": 252.66,
    "original_speaker": "SPEAKER_01",
    "verified_speaker": "Rinpochoe",
    "text": "When you're stuck in the New York traffic, or when you're in an elevator, or when you're on a bus, when you're travelling on an aeroplane etc, it's very easy simply to look within, to look at the mind.",
    "include_in_corpus": null,
    "exclusion_reason": null
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "SRR_001_24",
    "start": 273.908,
    "end": 286.183,
    "original_speaker": "SPEAKER_00",
    "verified_speaker": "Translator",
    "text": "Of course, when I say meditate like this, to look within, to look at the nature of mind, I'm not suggesting that you have to try to sit cross-legged and straighten your spine and put your hands in the meditation posture, etc.",
    "include_in_corpus": null,
    "exclusion_reason": null
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "SRR_001_25",
    "start": 286.263,
    "end": 286.744,
    "original_speaker": "SPEAKER_00",
    "verified_speaker": "Translator",
    "text": "Not at all.",
    "include_in_corpus": null,
    "exclusion_reason": null
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "SRR_001_26",
    "start": 287.104,
    "end": 288.967,
    "original_speaker": "SPEAKER_00",
    "verified_speaker": "Translator",
    "text": "Here one just simply looks within.",
    "include_in_corpus": null,
    "exclusion_reason": null
  },
  {
